{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: `per_exchange_budget = 300.0`. yalexs-ble retries an operation up to `DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS` (4) times, each a connect through bleak-retry-connector plus up to three writes waiting `RESPONSE_TIMEOUT` (10 s), so roughly 4 min in the worst case. 300 s sits above that, so the library's own timeouts claim a silent slot first. Covered in `test_provider_constants`.","re":4702859794}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: a set without a name now calls `clear_lock_credential` first (core's `_clear_credential` drops the stored name), then `set_lock_credential`. The set clears the slot on the lock anyway, so the only cost is one extra exchange, and only for nameless sets. Tests: `test_set_credential_without_a_name_clears_the_old_name_first` and `test_set_credential_with_a_name_does_not_clear_first`.","re":4702859800}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: `async_get_usercodes(self.managed_slots | set(slots or ()))`, with `test_hard_refresh_reads_managed_slots_and_the_asked_ones`.","re":4702859804}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Good catch, fixed in f7598b55: the listener now matches the event's `device_id` against `self.lock.device_id`, and falls back to the entity id only when the lock entity has no device. `test_activity_for_the_main_entity_reaches_the_secure_mode_entity` builds both entities on one device and fires the event with the main entity's id.","re":4702859821}
{"a":"drgreenbaum","b":"Fixed in f7598b55: the refusal test uses `pin_already_in_use`, and there are `communication_error` tests for the set and read paths (→ `LockOperationFailed`). I kept `TestNativeTransportContract` because it's the shared contract every service provider runs; it guards against a future core change that lets an `OSError` through, as Schlage's does. Happy to drop it if you'd rather not have it here.","re":4702859822}
